{"timestamp": "2026-08-21T10:44:14.144Z", "type": "WebSurferEvent", "source": "WebSurfer", "message": "\nThought #3: Open the Daytona announcement message to expose its full header, reactions, and thread metadata needed for counting reactions and replies.\nAction #3: executing tool 'left_click' with arguments {\"action\":\"left_click\",\"ref\":\"e73\",\"target\":{\"ref\":\"e73\",\"role\":\"listitem\",\"name\":\"Daytona: Spot GPU sandboxes are now live for everyone! Run GPU workloads on preemptible capacity at a fraction of on-demand pricing: • No quotas: spot GPUs don't count against your GPU quota. Available capacity is the only limit. . • Deeply discounted: significantly cheaper than on-demand GPUs, see the pricing page: [ https://www.daytona.io/pricing (link)] . • All GPU types: H100, H200, RTX Pro 6000, RTX 4090, RTX 5090, with ordered fallback between types. . Getting started: choose a GPU, set resources, and use any Docker image: sandbox = daytona.create( CreateSandboxFromImageParams( image=\\\"nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-base-ubuntu22.04\\\", auto_delete_interval=0, spot=True, resources=Resources(gpu=1, gpu_type=GpuType.H100), ) ) Heads up: spot sandboxes are preemptible. They can be reclaimed at any time when on-demand capacity is needed, so design workloads to tolerate interruption. Preempted sandboxes get a spotEvictedAt timestamp and stay retrievable for 24 hours. Try it: [ https://app.daytona.io/ (link)] Docs: [ https://www.daytona.io/docs/sandboxes#spot-gpu-sandboxes (link)] Questions? Drop them here or at [ support@daytona.io (link)] saluting face emoji. 8:38 AM. 4 links.\"},\"coordinate\":[871,837]}", "action": "left_click", "arguments": {"action": "left_click", "ref": "e73", "target": {"ref": "e73", "role": "listitem", "name": "Daytona: Spot GPU sandboxes are now live for everyone! Run GPU workloads on preemptible capacity at a fraction of on-demand pricing: • No quotas: spot GPUs don't count against your GPU quota. Available capacity is the only limit. . • Deeply discounted: significantly cheaper than on-demand GPUs, see the pricing page: [ https://www.daytona.io/pricing (link)] . • All GPU types: H100, H200, RTX Pro 6000, RTX 4090, RTX 5090, with ordered fallback between types. . Getting started: choose a GPU, set resources, and use any Docker image: sandbox = daytona.create( CreateSandboxFromImageParams( image=\"nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-base-ubuntu22.04\", auto_delete_interval=0, spot=True, resources=Resources(gpu=1, gpu_type=GpuType.H100), ) ) Heads up: spot sandboxes are preemptible. They can be reclaimed at any time when on-demand capacity is needed, so design workloads to tolerate interruption. Preempted sandboxes get a spotEvictedAt timestamp and stay retrievable for 24 hours. Try it: [ https://app.daytona.io/ (link)] Docs: [ https://www.daytona.io/docs/sandboxes#spot-gpu-sandboxes (link)] Questions? Drop them here or at [ support@daytona.io (link)] saluting face emoji. 8:38 AM. 4 links."}, "thoughts": "Open the Daytona announcement message to expose its full header, reactions, and thread metadata needed for counting reactions and replies."}, "url": "https://app.slack.com/client/T064SFP56MC/C08DJTEFUSX"}
